.Dd September 19, 2026
.Dt LOGIN 1
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm login
.Nd authenticate at the console and begin a session
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Ss os-real and installed root
.Nm
.Op Fl p
.Op Fl h Ar host
.Op Oo Fl f Oc Ar user
.Ss os-simple
.Nm
.Sh DESCRIPTION
The console uses
.Nm
to authenticate an account before starting its shell.
On both os-simple and os-real, init provides no unauthenticated shell
when
.Pa /bin/login
is absent.
.Ss BusyBox login
On os-real and the installed root,
.Pa /bin/login
is the BusyBox 1.36.1 applet from the set-id
.Ql busybox-suid
build.
Init's session child starts it.
.Pp
The options are:
.Bl -tag -width "-h host"
.It Fl f
Skip password authentication for the specified user.
Only root may use this option.
.It Fl h Ar host
Record the host the user came from.
.It Fl p
Preserve the environment, except that
.Ev HOME
and
.Ev SHELL
are set afresh,
.Ev USER
and
.Ev LOGNAME
too for an account other than root, and unsafe variables are removed from
a set-id invocation.
.El
.Pp
The
.Ev LOGIN_TIMEOUT
environment variable gives the timeout in seconds.
The default is 60; 0 disables the timeout.
.Pp
This build uses shadow passwords and BusyBox's SHA crypt support.
The securetty check, login scripts, and nologin feature are disabled.
The login shell reads
.Pa /etc/profile .
.Ss Project login
On os-simple,
.Pa /bin/login
is the project program, started as root by init-login.
It has no set-id bit.
Before prompting, it resets the terminal to canonical mode with echo
and discards pending input.
It does not create a session or claim the terminal; init's child has
already done both.
.Pp
The prompt is
.Ql "rach2 login: " .
The credential library reads the password without echo and verifies it
against
.Pa /etc/shadow .
An unknown name and an incorrect password produce the same diagnostic,
.Ql "login: incorrect" .
There is a two-second pause between failed attempts.
After three failed attempts,
.Nm
prints
.Ql "login: too many tries"
and exits; init starts it again.
A bare newline does not count as an attempt.
Names longer than 63 characters are discarded.
A partial name at end of input is terminated and processed by the same rule.
Password input reads terminal modes directly.
Only ENOTTY permits nonterminal input; any other mode-read error or a
failure to disable echo stops input.
Before prompting, the program closes descriptors 3 through 1023.
.Pp
After authentication,
.Nm
clears supplementary groups, sets the group ID, then sets the user ID.
A failure is fatal.
It enters the account's home directory, or falls back to
.Pa /
if that fails, and prints
.Pa /etc/motd .
.Pp
The new environment contains only
.Ev PATH ,
set to
.Ql /bin:/usr/bin ,
and
.Ev HOME ,
.Ev SHELL ,
.Ev USER ,
and
.Ev LOGNAME
from the account record.
The account's shell replaces
.Nm
as a login shell, with
.Ql -
followed by the shell's base name as
.Ql argv[0] .
.Sh FILES
.Bl -tag -width /etc/profile
.It Pa /etc/passwd
Account records.
.It Pa /etc/shadow
Password records.
.It Pa /etc/motd
Message of the day.
.It Pa /etc/profile
Read by the BusyBox login shell.
The project login does not read it.
.El
.Sh EXAMPLES
At the os-simple console prompt, enter
.Ql root
and then the account's password:
.Dl rach2 login: root
.Sh DIAGNOSTICS
The project login reports:
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Ql login: incorrect
The name or password was not accepted.
.It Ql login: too many tries
Three attempts failed.
.It Ql login: cannot become NAME: ERROR
Changing the supplementary groups, group ID, or user ID failed.
.It Ql login: DIR: ERROR; using /
The home directory could not be entered.
.It Ql login: cannot exec SHELL: ERROR
The account's shell could not be executed.
.El
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr passwd 1 ,
.Xr sh 1 ,
.Xr su 1 ,
.Xr passwd 5 ,
.Xr shadow 5
